WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.750
- May 26th is Red Nose Day on NBC.

00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:04.470
It's a great cause that's helped out

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:06.370
millions of kids over the years.

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:08.670
And here to tell us more
about it is none other than

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:13.144
People Magazine's reigning
sexiest man alive, Paul Rudd.

00:00:13.144 --> 00:00:15.894
(exciting music)

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:20.437
I love it, nice to see you Paul.

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:22.223
So where are you calling from?

00:00:22.223 --> 00:00:23.490
- Nice to see you, Kelly.

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:24.650
- [Kelly] Where are you calling from?

00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:25.630
- New York.

00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:26.463
- [Kelly] Oh, okay.

00:00:26.463 --> 00:00:28.130
- Calling from New York.
- Right on.

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:30.640
Tell us more about Red Nose Day, Paul.

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:34.060
- Well, Red Nose Day is
this amazing organization

00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:39.060
that was started in
2015 by Richard Curtis,

00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:42.770
who is a great writer and
director that many people know.

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:46.920
But it supports all kinds
of kids all over the world

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:49.990
with lots of programs,
makes sure that they're safe

00:00:49.990 --> 00:00:53.470
and they're healthy and
educated and empowered.

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:57.700
And since then, they've
helped over 30 million kids.

00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:02.080
They've raised 275 million dollars

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:06.250
from people everywhere
donating to this, incredible.

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:08.120
- Yeah, I've worked with them for years.

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:10.370
It's the coolest, coolest organization.

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:12.240
It actually makes a huge impact.

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:14.350
How did you get involved?

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:18.480
- I was invited years ago by Richard

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:21.140
and I was really, you know,

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:23.740
one, they put together these
shows and they're really funny.

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:28.530
And I got to do a fun sketch
where I played Danny Hall,

00:01:28.530 --> 00:01:31.380
the male version of Annie Hall.

00:01:33.287 --> 00:01:34.960
And it was a lot of fun and it was funny

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:36.680
and it was all part of this show.

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:38.760
And with every year, I started getting

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:39.660
more and more involved

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:40.840
because I was just so impressed

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:45.120
with what Red Nose Day was all about.

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:46.980
And I got to go to Maine

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:50.174
and this was where things really became,

00:01:50.174 --> 00:01:52.566
(phone dings)
that's my, I got an email.

00:01:52.566 --> 00:01:53.763
- Hey, you got an email, Paul.

00:01:55.319 --> 00:01:59.550
- This is where things got
really, you know, major for me

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:02.980
because I got to go to Maine
and really see firsthand

00:02:03.910 --> 00:02:07.810
what kind of impact these
donations were making.

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:08.643
You know, so many times,

00:02:08.643 --> 00:02:11.790
we give our money to different charities

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:12.820
and it's an incredible thing

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:15.530
but we don't really get to
see, up close and personal,

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:18.080
the difference that they're
making, our donations.

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:20.300
And I got to go to
Maine and go to a school

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:23.240
and meet a lot of kids that were,

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:25.610
you know, they were food insecure.

00:02:25.610 --> 00:02:28.750
They needed to be, they needed help.

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:31.750
And all of these kids were being fed

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:35.080
and food was provided
through Red Nose Day.

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:37.130
I met all of these amazing workers there,

00:02:37.130 --> 00:02:38.080
people in the school,

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:40.540
and it had such a profound impact on me

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:44.801
that I just wanted to stay
involved in whatever way I could.

00:02:44.801 --> 00:02:46.140
- You're absolutely right, man.

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:47.250
It's a different thing.

00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:48.780
Like, you know, we give money to things

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:50.390
and sometimes you don't know where it goes

00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:51.530
and I've been involved in that since too.

00:02:51.530 --> 00:02:52.710
That's why I love Red Nose Day,

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:53.990
because I've actually seen,

00:02:53.990 --> 00:02:55.830
how you saw the direct impact in Maine,

00:02:55.830 --> 00:02:56.970
you see the direct impact.

00:02:56.970 --> 00:02:58.900
Like not only on the kids that it impacts,

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:00.870
but their families, it's
the domino effect of it.

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:03.220
And it's a really, really
beautiful thing to be a part of.

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:04.440
It's a great cause.

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:06.770
Thank you so much for giving us a call

00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:08.163
and I love your wallpaper.

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:11.590
- Thanks so much.

00:03:11.590 --> 00:03:12.847
- [Kelly] I dig it.

00:03:12.847 --> 00:03:13.680
- Get your (indistinct).

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:15.090
- Oh yeah, I feel left out.

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:19.677
I love it, bye Paul,
talk to you next time.

